# MONITOR HOOK - run when a node reports a state
#
#        none of the methods is mandatory. When a node reports a state, the
#        state's dots and spaces become underscores and a method of that name
#        is called if the class defines one, with name=<node>:
#
#        install.prescript -> install_prescript(name)
#        install.success   -> install_success(name)
#
#        each returns <True|False>,"message"
#
#        The methods are called on the class, not on an instance: __init__ never
#        runs, so keep state out of it.
#
# Loaded by name, plugins/hooks/monitor/node.py. There is no search path.
